    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner`.\n\n**What changed** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`):\n\n1. Wrapped the derived code in a new `deduplicateCustomerCode(...)` step:\n   ```java\n   owner.setCustomerCode(deduplicateCustomerCode(deriveCustomerCode(owner)));\n   ```\n\n2. Added the `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper: it gathers the customerCodes of all existing owners and, if the base code is already taken, appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2`, incrementing until it finds a value no existing owner holds. If the base code is free it is returned unchanged.\n\n3. Added the needed imports (`java.util.Objects`, `java.util.stream.Collectors`).\n\nThis follows the same \"evaluated before persist, over `ownerRepository.findAll()`\" pattern used by the surrounding collision/limit checks (namesakes, household members, city capacity). It only runs when the owner has no pre-supplied customerCode, matching the existing `if (owner.getCustomerCode() == null)` guard.\n\n**Tests:** the full suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique`) passes \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
